{"availability":"available","full":"amap-cvlab/ABot-Recon","name":"ABot-Recon","description":"Streaming 3D reconstruction from only video input: Revisiting Local Context for Long-Horizon Streaming 3D Reconstruction","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1376,"forks":74,"created":"2026-08-27T08:32:09Z","updated":"2026-10-14T16:10:58Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://amap-cvlab.github.io/ABot-Recon-html/","topics":["3d-reconstruction","abot-recon","slam"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/acvlab/abot-recon-streaming-3d","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:01.931Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:01.931Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:01.931Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:17.765Z","stars":1288,"forks":70},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:01.931Z","stars":1376,"forks":74}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["In one sentence: ABot-Recon reconstructs long video streams with a fixed 12-frame local context, composing current-frame geometry and adjacent relative poses into a global reconstruction without persistent learned long-range memory.","Long-horizon streaming reconstruction is often approached by adding increasingly elaborate mechanisms for retaining and fusing long-range state. ABot-Recon takes a deliberately local route. At each time step, it solves the same bounded prediction problem:","This design keeps model-state memory and per-frame computation independent of the elapsed sequence length. A lightweight motion-visual rotation refiner and composition-aware pose loss are used to limit drift when local poses are composed over long horizons."],"features":["cache KV features from the preceding 11 frames;","predict a point map $Pi$ in the current camera coordinate system;","estimate the adjacent relative pose $T{i-1\\leftarrow i}$; and","recover the global trajectory and point cloud through sequential pose composition."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.